    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1972-p31.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(2^6=64\\equiv-1\\pmod{13},\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} 2^{1000}&=2^{6\\cdot166+4}\\\\ &\\equiv(-1)^{166}2^4\\\\ &\\equiv16\\\\ &\\equiv3\\pmod{13}. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(2^6\\equiv-1\\pmod{13}\\)",
        "Write \\(1000=6\\cdot166+4\\)"
      ],
